  'ニュースを|大きさを|通じて|地震の被害の': { order: [1, 3, 4, 2], starSlot: 3, starChoice: 4, translation: 'It was through the radio news that I first learned the magnitude of the earthquake damage.' },
  'と|手伝える|なると|人がいない': { order: [2, 4, 1, 3], starSlot: 3, starChoice: 1, translation: 'If it turns out that there is no one who can help no matter who I ask, I have no choice but to do it alone.' },
  'でも|では|食べない|ダイエット中': { order: [4, 1, 3, 2], starSlot: 3, starChoice: 3, translation: 'If a feast is served right in front of me, no matter how much I am on a diet, I cannot help but eat.' },
  '効くが|人に|アレルギー|よっては': { order: [1, 2, 4, 3], starSlot: 3, starChoice: 4, translation: 'This medicine is very effective, but caution is required because it causes allergies depending on the person.' },
  '予想した|基づいて|結果|に': { order: [4, 2, 1, 3], starSlot: 3, starChoice: 1, translation: 'As a result of forecasting based on the data of the past ten years, the number of children will likely continue to decrease.' },
  'また忘れて|ことか|注意された|わからないのに': { order: [3, 2, 4, 1], starSlot: 2, starChoice: 2, translation: 'Even though I don\'t know how many times I have been cautioned not to forget my homework, I ended up forgetting it again.' },
  'あわてて|にせよ|ばかなことを|いた': { order: [1, 4, 2, 3], starSlot: 2, starChoice: 4, translation: 'Even granting that I was in a panic at that time, I regret having done such a foolish thing.' },
  'しっかりしていても|兄のほうが|よい|いえば': { order: [4, 2, 1, 3], starSlot: 3, starChoice: 1, translation: 'Judging by age, the older brother should be the more dependable one, and yet the younger brother is more reliable.' },
